From: AX6 local correctness review <local@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] nss-dp: start every TX queue after successful activation

The IPQ807x takeover path disables all TX queues even when the port is
administratively down. Resuming such a port cannot rely on
netif_device_attach(), which only wakes queues for a running device.
The later successful ndo_open must restore all queues, not only TXQ0.

Keep this in the existing successful activation path. Failed opens and
quarantined ports must retain the closed admission and stopped queues.
Do not change the non-IPQ807x path or retire any firmware/DMA resources.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/nss_dp_main.c
+++ b/nss_dp_main.c
@@ -483,7 +483,7 @@ void nss_dp_activate_data_plane(struct nss_dp_dev *dp)
 		dp->link_state = __NSS_DP_LINK_UP;
 		netif_carrier_on(dp->netdev);
 	}
-	netif_start_queue(dp->netdev);
+	netif_tx_start_all_queues(dp->netdev);
 }
 #endif
 
